    "notes": "Retrained at the corrected geometry (issue #36). state_len=4 means the CRF emits target[4:]; the 48-nt target puts those four sacrificial bases in the oligo's constant prefix so the full 27-nt code is emitted, where the previous 40-nt target discarded the code's first four bases and discriminated on 23 nt. Measured accuracy-neutral at 16-plex across 4 geometries x 3 seeds \u2014 the 16-plex is not discrimination-limited \u2014 but it restores the separability the 96-code pool was designed for, which an 80-plex needs. Match decodes against the EMITTED references shipped in the bundle, never the full-length targets. The pilot is CONFOUNDED (each nbc on exactly one flowcell): report two 8x8 matrices, never one 16x16."
